        "original_id": "4f641eff-66de-591c-b20e-cd8e4b7b1842",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Levinson, William Link, Bruce Geller, Joe Mannix, Gail Fisher, Peggy Fair\n- TV Series: Mannix\n- Roles: private investigator, secretary\n- Awards: Golden Globe Awards, Emmy Award\n\nFacts:\n- Bruce Geller was born on October 13, 1930, and he was an American lyricist, screenwriter, director, and television producer.\n- Mannix was created by Richard Levinson and William Link and developed by executive producer Bruce Geller.\n- Joe Mannix is the title character of Mannix, and he is a private investigator.\n- Gail Fisher played secretary Peggy Fair on the television detective series Mannix from 1968 through 1975.\n- Gail Fisher won two Golden Globe Awards and an Emmy Award for her role as Peggy Fair on Mannix.\n- Gail Fisher was the first black woman to win either a Golden Globe Award or an Emmy Award.\n- Bruce Geller died on May 21, 1978.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
